<title>ESTONIA: HOIU LIISING SIGNS SYNDICATED LOAN AGREEMENT.</title>
<headline>HOIU LIISING SIGNS SYNDICATED LOAN AGREEMENT.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hoiupanga Liising, the leasing arm of Hoiupank , said on Wednesday it signed an agreement with German banks to receive a syndicated loan of three million marks.</p>
<p>The loan, which matures in three years, has an interest rate of mark LIBOR plus a margin of one percent, it added in a statement.</p>
<p>The loan organiser was Landesbank Schleswig-Holstein with Landesbank Rheinland-Pfalz.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn newsroom, +372 6209 201, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
</text>
